        "## 3. Methodology\n",
        "Assumptions & Definitions:\n",
        "\n",
        "Features: The model utilizes gsc_impressions and gsc_avg_position as the primary indicators of a page's current visibility and potential.\n",
        "\n",
        "Target Label: gsc_clicks is used as the target variable to represent the realized value (opportunity score proxy).\n",
        "\n",
        "Model: A RandomForestRegressor was selected to capture non-linear relationships between position, impressions, and expected clicks.\n",
        "\n",
        "Validation Design & Leakage Checks:\n",
        "Initially, a standard random train/test split was used as a baseline. However, this approach is fundamentally flawed for multi-client data, as pages from the same client can leak into both the training and testing sets, leading to over-optimistic results. To ensure an honest evaluation, a strict GroupShuffleSplit was implemented, grouped by client_hash_id. This guarantees that the model is tested on entirely unseen clients.\n",
        "\n",
        "Furthermore, a leakage audit was conducted between impressions and clicks. While there is a strong synchronous correlation (impressions limit the maximum possible clicks), this overlap is acceptable because the model functions as a directional ranking tool for existing pages, not a strict forecaster of future traffic."
      ],
      "id": "2TdTthLkCXq-"
    },
